00:17:28,679 --> 00:17:33,799
strange to them. There now came a lull in his look as he silently turned over

208
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:38,999
the leaves of the book once more and at last standing motionless with closed

209
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:44,519
eyes for the moment seemed communing with God in himself. But again he leaned

210
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:49,318
towards the people and bowing his head lowly with an aspect of the deepest yet

211
00:17:49,319 --> 00:17:53,478
manliest humility. He spake these words.

212
00:17:53,479 --> 00:18:00,438
Shipmates, God has laid but one hand upon you. both his hands press upon me.

213
00:18:00,439 --> 00:18:05,398
I have read you by what murky light may be mine the lesson that Jonah teaches to

214
00:18:05,399 --> 00:18:10,919
all sinners and therefore to you and still more to me for I am a greater

215
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:16,358
sinner than you. And now, how gladly would I come down from this mast head

216
00:18:16,359 --> 00:18:20,839
and sit on the hatches there where you sit and listen as you listen, while

217
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:26,038
someone of you reads me that other and more awful lesson which Jonah teaches to

218
00:18:26,039 --> 00:18:32,119
me as a pilot of the living God. How being anointed pilot, prophet, or

219
00:18:32,120 --> 00:18:37,158
speaker of true things and bidden by the Lord to sound those unwelcome truths in

220
00:18:37,159 --> 00:18:42,119
the ears of a wicked Nineveh, Jonah, appalled at the hostility he should

221
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:47,238
raise, fled from his mission, and sought to escape his duty and his God by taking

222
00:18:47,239 --> 00:18:50,518
ship at Jopa. But God is everywhere.

223
00:18:50,519 --> 00:18:56,119
Tarsish he never reached. As we have seen, God came upon him in the whale and

224
00:18:56,120 --> 00:19:01,317
swallowed him down to the living gulfs of doom, and with swift slantings tore

225
00:19:01,318 --> 00:19:06,598
him along into the midst of the seas, where the eddying depths sucked him

226
00:19:06,599 --> 00:19:11,798
10,000 fathoms down, and the weeds were wrapped about his head, and all the

227
00:19:11,799 --> 00:19:17,317
watery world of woe bowled over him. Yet even then, beyond the reach of any

228
00:19:17,318 --> 00:19:22,518
plummet, out of the belly of hell, when the whale grounded upon the ocean's

229
00:19:22,519 --> 00:19:27,557
utmost bones, even then God heard the engulfed repenting prophet when he

230
00:19:27,558 --> 00:19:33,158
cried. Then God spake unto the fish, and from the shuddering cold and blackness

231
00:19:33,159 --> 00:19:38,119
of the sea, the whale came breaching up towards the warm and pleasant sun, and

232
00:19:38,120 --> 00:19:43,637
all the delights of air and earth, and vomited out Jonah upon the dry land.

233
00:19:43,638 --> 00:19:49,557
When the word of the Lord came a second time, and Jonah bruised and beaten, his

234
00:19:49,558 --> 00:19:55,158
ears like two seashells still multitudinously murmuring of the ocean.

235
00:19:55,159 --> 00:20:00,518
Jonah did the Almighty's bidding. And what was that, shipmates? To preach the

236
00:20:00,519 --> 00:20:06,119
truth to the face of falsehood. That was it. This, shipmates, is the other

237
00:20:06,120 --> 00:20:11,397
lesson. And woe to that pilot of the living God who slight it. Woe to him

238
00:20:11,398 --> 00:20:14,999
whom this world charms from gospel duty.

239
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:19,397
Woe to him who seeks to pour oil upon the waters when God has brooded them

240
00:20:19,398 --> 00:20:25,798
into a gale. Woe to him who seeks to please rather than to appall. Woe to him

241
00:20:25,799 --> 00:20:31,158
whose good name is more to him than goodness. Woe to him who in this world

242
00:20:31,159 --> 00:20:37,317
courts not dishonor. Woe to him who would not be true even though to be

243
00:20:37,318 --> 00:20:43,637
false were salvation. Yay! Woe to him who, as the great Pilate Paul has it,

244
00:20:43,638 --> 00:20:49,599
while preaching to others, is himself a castaway.

245
00:20:49,638 --> 00:20:53,717
He dropped and fell away from himself for a moment, then lifting his face to

246
00:20:53,718 --> 00:20:58,199
them again, showed a deep joy in his eyes, as he cried out with a heavenly

247
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:04,358
enthusiasm, "But oh shipmates, on the starboard hand of every woe there is a

248
00:21:04,359 --> 00:21:09,477
sure delight, and higher the top of that delight, than the bottom of the woe is

249
00:21:09,478 --> 00:21:15,717
deep." Is not the main truck higher than the Kelson is low? Delight is to him a

250
00:21:15,718 --> 00:21:21,317
far, far upward and inward delight, who against the proud gods and commodors of

251
00:21:21,318 --> 00:21:27,158
this earth ever stands forth his own inexurable self. Delight is to him whose

252
00:21:27,159 --> 00:21:32,279
strong arms yet support him when the ship of this base treacherous world has

253
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:37,557
gone down beneath him. Delight it is to him who gives no quarter in the truth

254
00:21:37,558 --> 00:21:42,358
and kills, burns, and destroys all sin, though he pluck it out from under the

255
00:21:42,359 --> 00:21:47,878
robes of senators and judges. Delight, top, gallant delight is to him who

256
00:21:47,879 --> 00:21:53,477
acknowledges no law or lord but the Lord his God, and is only a patriot to

257
00:21:53,478 --> 00:21:59,317
heaven. Delight is to him whom all the waves of the billows of the seas and the

258
00:21:59,318 --> 00:22:04,759
boisterous mob can never shake from this sure keel of the ages. An eternal

259
00:22:04,760 --> 00:22:06,999
delight and deliciousness will be his.

260
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:13,158
Who coming to lay him down can say with his final breath, oh father, chiefly

261
00:22:13,159 --> 00:22:18,999
known to me by thy rod, mortal or immortal, here I die. I have striven to

262
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:25,158
be thine more than to be this world's or mine own. Yet this is nothing. I leave

263
00:22:25,159 --> 00:22:32,679
eternity to thee. For what is man that he should live out the lifetime of his God?

264
00:22:32,680 --> 00:22:37,638
He said no more, but slowly, waving a benediction, covered his face with his

265
00:22:37,639 --> 00:22:43,158
hands, and so remained kneeling till all the people had departed, and he was left

266
00:22:43,159 --> 00:22:46,879
alone in the place.
